WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.169 --> 00:00:04.671
Dear Edward
is this story that is

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:06.506
born out of
this tragic circumstance.

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:10.219
I got you. Come here.

00:00:11.595 --> 00:00:12.721
You’re gonna be okay.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.059
There’s a deadly plane crash
and the only survivor

00:00:17.059 --> 00:00:19.478
is a 12 year-old child
named Edward

00:00:19.478 --> 00:00:21.772
who is my character’s nephew.

00:00:22.606 --> 00:00:24.358
What happened
isn’t fair, Edward.

00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:27.319
I know I will never
replace your mom. 

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:31.823
Lacey’s wanted to have a child.
It’s been a struggle that’s

00:00:31.823 --> 00:00:34.451
affected her marriage, her
self-esteem, everything.

00:00:34.451 --> 00:00:37.204
And then suddenly
out of this tragic event,

00:00:37.204 --> 00:00:39.790
there’s a boy who
drops into her lap.

00:00:40.499 --> 00:00:42.167
And then her life
starts to change and

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:43.752
all this really
beautiful stuff happens.

00:00:44.211 --> 00:00:47.214
The airline will
pay for a psychologist.

00:00:47.214 --> 00:00:48.882
I think it could
be a good idea. 

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:51.134
There’s this
grief group community

00:00:51.134 --> 00:00:54.513
that comes from other people
who have experienced this loss.

00:00:54.513 --> 00:00:56.848
Did you say a 12 year-old
boy named Edward?

00:00:56.848 --> 00:00:58.016
Is it “the” Edward?

00:00:58.016 --> 00:00:59.434
Are you the aunt?

00:01:00.269 --> 00:01:02.521
Yeah. Yeah, that’s me.

00:01:02.521 --> 00:01:04.022
I guess I’m the aunt. 

00:01:04.022 --> 00:01:05.482
How’s he doing?

00:01:06.108 --> 00:01:06.858
How’re you doing?

00:01:06.858 --> 00:01:07.859
(Inhale)

00:01:08.402 --> 00:01:11.363
As disparate as
the experiences are,

00:01:11.363 --> 00:01:14.741
this point of grief
connects lives

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:16.660
that would never
have known each other.

00:01:17.536 --> 00:01:22.207
Dee Dee is someone who
thinks that she's got it all.

00:01:22.416 --> 00:01:23.917
Hi.

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:25.961
With the death of her husband,

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:27.879
gradually discovers,

00:01:28.422 --> 00:01:29.923
none of it is real.

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:32.843
He thought that he was gonna
turn things around financially

00:01:32.843 --> 00:01:35.345
for you guys. I- 
I know he was working on that.

00:01:36.138 --> 00:01:40.100
Because the inciting incident of
the show is so tragic,

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.352
people might think that it’s
gonna be depressing.

00:01:42.352 --> 00:01:46.189
But really, it is about
watching people

00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:47.441
be resilient.

00:01:48.984 --> 00:01:50.861
They find love,

00:01:50.861 --> 00:01:52.237
they find connection.

00:01:52.237 --> 00:01:56.241
It reminds you of just how
surprising life can be.

00:01:58.577 --> 00:02:00.203
You can come back from anything,

00:02:00.203 --> 00:02:02.831
if you have enough love and
support around you.

00:02:05.459 --> 00:02:09.921
In the face of grief, the only
way that we go on is hope.

00:02:14.259 --> 00:02:17.471
♪♪

